    "durationMs": 200894,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. \n\n**What I built** (workspace was empty, so everything is new):\n- `app/` — FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM (`links` table: id, unique code, url, clicks, created_at) and pydantic-settings reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment, forced onto the psycopg3 driver\n- `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` — migration `0001_create_links`, URL taken from `DATABASE_URL` at runtime, never hard-coded\n- `start.sh` — runs `python -m alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (uses `python -m` forms since the console scripts aren't on PATH here)\n- `requirements.txt` (pinned to installed versions, no extras added) and `README.md` with start instructions\n\n**Verification results** — a 76-check httpx suite passed 76/0 on a clean database, covering: auto/custom code creation (201, URL echoed byte-for-byte including query/fragment), duplicate code 409 with `error` field, unknown-code 404s, 302 redirects incrementing clicks exactly once (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`), ascending creation order via autoincrement id, malformed JSON/empty body/missing/invalid url (no scheme, ftp, no host)/invalid code (length, charset, type) all returning 422 with `error`, and boundary codes 4–20 chars. I also confirmed via a real `sh start.sh` restart that links and click counts survive (clicks=3 before restart → still 3, next redirect → 4), and that `alembic upgrade head` is idempotent on second boot.\n\nThe `bench` database is left pristine (migrated schema, zero rows), the test server is stopped, and files are uncommitted for your review."
